---
import DefaultLayout from "@/Layouts/DefaultLayout.astro";
---

<DefaultLayout
	title="The Johto Region — Animancy Website Starter"
	description="Explore the historic Johto region. A clean website example demonstrating the Animancy template system."
>
	<main class="container flow-large home-container">
		<!-- HERO SECTION -->
		<section class="johto-about flow hero-section">
			<header class="flow header-flow">
				<div>
					<span class="tag">Example Website</span>
				</div>
				<h1 class="fs-step-7 hero-title">
					Welcome to the Johto Region
				</h1>
				<p class="fs-step-1 lead hero-description">
					The Johto region, a land where tradition and history blend harmoniously with the wonders of Pokémon,
					welcomes trainers from around the world. Located west of Kanto, Johto offers a journey through ancient
					traditions, sacred towers, and untamed wilderness.
				</p>
			</header>

			<!-- REGION FEATURES -->
			<article class="region-features flow-large content-flow">
				<!-- TRADITION -->
				<section class="tradition flow section-flow">
					<h2 class="fs-step-4 section-heading">A Land of Tradition</h2>
					<p class="fs-step-0 text-block">
						Johto prides itself on preserving the ways of old. From the sacred Bell Tower in Ecruteak City where the
						legendary Ho-Oh is said to perch, to the Ruins of Alph with their mysterious Unown inscriptions, history
						echoes throughout the region. Our cities maintain traditional architecture, with Ecruteak City's dance
						theaters and Violet City's Sprout Tower standing as testaments to our cultural heritage.
					</p>
				</section>

				<!-- CITIES & LANDMARKS -->
				<section class="cities flow section-flow-lg">
					<h2 class="fs-step-4 section-heading">Cities & Landmarks</h2>
					<p class="fs-step-0 intro-text">Explore our diverse cities, each with unique charm and character:</p>
					<ul role="list" class="flow city-list">
						<li><strong>New Bark Town</strong> - Where new beginnings blow like the wind</li>
						<li><strong>Violet City</strong> - Home to the swaying Sprout Tower and the region's first Gym</li>
						<li><strong>Azalea Town</strong> - Known for its Slowpoke Well and masterful Poké Ball craftsman</li>
						<li><strong>Goldenrod City</strong> - The bustling metropolis featuring the Radio Tower and Department Store</li>
						<li><strong>Ecruteak City</strong> - Where legend and history intertwine at the Burned and Bell Towers</li>
						<li><strong>Olivine City</strong> - A port city with a magnificent lighthouse guarded by Jasmine</li>
						<li><strong>Cianwood City</strong> - An isolated coastal town famous for its pharmacy</li>
						<li><strong>Mahogany Town</strong> - A small, quiet town with a dark secret</li>
						<li><strong>Blackthorn City</strong> - Nestled among mountains, home to dragon tamers</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<!-- POKEMON LEAGUE CARDS -->
				<section class="pokemon-league flow section-flow-lg">
					<h2 class="fs-step-4 section-heading">Featured Landmarks</h2>
					<div class="grid landmarks-grid" data-cols="2">
						<div class="card">
							<div class="image"></div>
							<div class="content">
								<a href="#">
									<span class="title">Ecruteak Bell Tower</span>
								</a>
								<p class="desc">
									Explore the sacred tower towering over Ecruteak City, built as a sign of friendship between humans and Pokémon.
								</p>
								<a class="action" href="#">
									Find out more
									<span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
								</a>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="card">
							<div class="image"></div>
							<div class="content">
								<a href="#">
									<span class="title">Ruins of Alph</span>
								</a>
								<p class="desc">
									Investigate ancient stone chambers filled with enigmatic Unown hieroglyphs and timeless mysteries.
								</p>
								<a class="action" href="#">
									Find out more
									<span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
								</a>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="card">
							<div class="image"></div>
							<div class="content">
								<a href="#">
									<span class="title">Goldenrod Radio Tower</span>
								</a>
								<p class="desc">
									Visit Johto's broadcast headquarters, broadcasting music and news across the entire region.
								</p>
								<a class="action" href="#">
									Find out more
									<span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
								</a>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="card">
							<div class="image"></div>
							<div class="content">
								<a href="#">
									<span class="title">Lake of Rage</span>
								</a>
								<p class="desc">
									A serene mountain lake steeped in rumor and home to legendary dragon-type Pokémon encounters.
								</p>
								<a class="action" href="#">
									Find out more
									<span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
								</a>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>

				<!-- LEGENDARY ENCOUNTERS -->
				<section class="legendary-pokemon flow section-flow">
					<h2 class="fs-step-4 section-heading">Legendary Encounters</h2>
					<p class="fs-step-0 text-block">
						Johto is blessed by the presence of legendary Pokémon that have shaped our region's mythology. The Tower
						Duo of Ho-Oh and Lugia watch over the skies and seas, while the elusive beasts Entei, Raikou, and Suicune
						roam our lands. Those deemed worthy may even encounter the time-traveling Celebi in the depths of Ilex
						Forest.
					</p>
				</section>
			</article>

			<!-- CALL TO ACTION -->
			<aside class="visitor-info flow cta-card">
				<h2 class="fs-step-4 cta-title">Plan Your Journey</h2>
				<p class="fs-step-0 cta-text">
					Whether you're a new trainer setting out from Professor Elm's laboratory or a seasoned Pokémon Master
					seeking new challenges, Johto welcomes you. Pack your Poké Balls, prepare your team, and embark on an
					unforgettable adventure through our historic region.
				</p>
				<nav class="journey-navigation">
					<a href="/playground" class="btn btn--primary" aria-label="Explore the design system playground">
						Explore Design System Playground →
					</a>
				</nav>
			</aside>
		</section>
	</main>
</DefaultLayout>

<style>
	.home-container {
		--space: 3.5rem;
		padding-block: 2.5rem 5rem;
	}

	.hero-section {
		--space: 1.5rem;
	}

	.header-flow {
		--space: 0.75rem;
	}

	.hero-title {
		margin: 0;
		font-weight: 800;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	}

	.hero-description {
		max-width: 65ch;
		opacity: 0.85;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.content-flow {
		--space: 3rem;
	}

	.section-flow {
		--space: 0.75rem;
	}

	.section-flow-lg {
		--space: 1.25rem;
	}

	.section-heading {
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.text-block {
		max-width: 75ch;
		opacity: 0.85;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.intro-text {
		opacity: 0.85;
	}

	.city-list {
		--space: 0.5rem;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	.landmarks-grid {
		--gutter: 1.5rem;
		--grid-min-item-size: 16rem;
	}

	.cta-card {
		--space: 1.25rem;
		padding: 2rem;
		border-radius: 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-weak);
		background: var(--background);
	}

	.cta-title {
		margin: 0;
		font-weight: 800;
	}

	.cta-text {
		margin: 0;
		opacity: 0.85;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
</style>
